Linux commands :
    1) ls(used to list files) - ls -l(long lighting format,- for perrmission),ls -la(all files ,hidden f),(dot . 'hidden'). 
    2) cd - change directory, .. (move 1 back), ~ (go home)
    3) cat - display file content , combine multi files , cat /path/"f" (for full path),
    4) file - determine the type of a file
    5) du - estimate and track the space consumed by files
    6) find - search for files ,./* (human readable),-type f(regular f),-user (user name),-group(group name),-size (000 c , c=bits),-executable(! for not executable), find / (rood directory)
    7) grep - search text patterns (find specific string, filters output)
    8) exit -to exit
    9) clear - clear terminal
    10) man - command manual, q (quit)
     
